    "created_at": "2019-09-24T08:01:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-24T08:01:12Z",
    "body": "> Well, consider a slight modification of your case, where the element's value has been given some LTR text. (Either via the user typing, or via a value=\"\" attribute.) In that case the border should definitely be red, right?\r\n\r\nSure, but then the placeholder isn't used for rendering. If the user types ltr it should switch from green to red, but that's the same as if the value is rtl and the user deletes it and writes ltr.",
